# The whole backdrop: a sliced sun over a perspective grid. 320x384, drawn at
# 2x to fill the 640x768 window exactly.
#
# One image rather than layers, because nothing here parallaxes — the camera
# never moves in a four-lane rhythm game, so a layered background would be
# machinery with no motion to justify it.
#
# The horizontal slices through the sun are doing the heavy lifting. They cost
# nothing, they are pure palette, and they place the whole game in a decade
# faster than any amount of shading would.
name rhythm-horizon
size 320 384
key a night-0
key b night-1
key c night-2
key d night-3-rim
key s sun-1
key t sun-0
key P neon-pink-0
key G grid-dim
pixels
*4 








































































































































